<title>BELGIUM: Fischler says Bulgaria now able to buy EU wheat.</title>
<headline>Fischler says Bulgaria now able to buy EU wheat.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria should now be able to buy 100,000 tonnes of EU intervention bread wheat to ensure sufficient supplies until the next harvest, EU Farm Commissioner Franz Fischler said on Wednedsday.</p>
<p>Fischler told farm ministers that Bulgaria had received IMF budgetary support and World Bank aid to make essential imports, EU officials said.</p>
<p>Germany, backed by France, Greece and the Netherlands, pressed the Commission to provide Bulgaria with six-months credit to buy the wheat at a &quot;reasonable&quot; price.</p>
<p>They asked the Commission to prepare a global estimate of Bulgaria's food needs.</p>
<p>Fischler requested member states to supply details of national food aid programmes for Bulgaria.</p>
</text>
